WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.702
Good morning, listeners.

2
00:00:03.652 --> 00:00:07.488
Today is October 29, 2026.

3
00:00:07.488 --> 00:00:14.976
Overnight, the S and P 500, Nasdaq, and Dow edged higher after a choppy Federal Reserve session.

4
00:00:14.976 --> 00:00:22.182
The S and P 500 gained twenty-one points, or zero point two eight percent, printing a bullish doji.

5
00:00:22.182 --> 00:00:29.179
However, Nasdaq 100 futures tumbled after hours as mega-cap tech earnings rattled investor sentiment.

6
00:00:29.179 --> 00:00:34.976
The Federal Reserve held interest rates steady between three point seven five and four percent.

7
00:00:34.976 --> 00:00:40.699
That ten-to-two vote matched consensus, yet revealed a hawkish shift inside the committee.

8
00:00:40.699 --> 00:00:47.366
Governor Cook and Cleveland Fed President Hammack dissented, demanding an immediate twenty-five-basis-point hike.

9
00:00:47.366 --> 00:00:54.951
Because traders feared three or more dissenters, two-year Treasury yields briefly slipped below four point seven percent.

10
00:00:54.951 --> 00:01:01.851
Still, the policy statement upgraded economic growth from solid to strong while flagging elevated inflation.

11
00:01:01.851 --> 00:01:10.429
Four forces are driving inflation: surging energy costs, tariffs, resilient consumer spending, and massive A I demand.

12
00:01:10.429 --> 00:01:16.937
Fed Chair Kevin Warsh offered zero forward guidance for December and dismissed midterm election pressures.

13
00:01:16.937 --> 00:01:23.297
Yet derivatives markets now price in consecutive twenty-five-basis-point hikes over the next two meetings.

14
00:01:23.297 --> 00:01:28.800
The central bank also kept bank reserves ample and reformed its future meeting calendar.

15
00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:36.949
Starting in 2027, one annual meeting will drop rate votes for strategy reviews, rising to two in 2028.

16
00:01:36.949 --> 00:01:42.341
Across the border, the Bank of Canada hiked rates by twenty-five basis points.

17
00:01:42.341 --> 00:01:48.322
That move defended the Canadian dollar below one point four zero to block imported inflation.

18
00:01:48.322 --> 00:01:55.197
In the United States, October consumer confidence rebounded from eighty-four point two to ninety-one point seven.

19
00:01:55.197 --> 00:02:01.569
Yet September C P I remains stuck at three point seven percent, pressuring household budgets.

20
00:02:01.569 --> 00:02:07.893
Tomorrow's September P C E inflation report is the ultimate macro catalyst for market direction.

21
00:02:07.893 --> 00:02:14.069
An upside inflation surprise would shatter the Fed's pause and crush high-valuation growth stocks.

22
00:02:14.069 --> 00:02:21.275
Geopolitical risks also cloud the outlook as Vice President Vance contacts Iranian hardliners for peace talks.

23
00:02:21.275 --> 00:02:28.481
The U S-Iran conflict has already cost forty-seven billion dollars, or two thousand dollars per American household.

24
00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:35.356
If talks fail, post-midterm strikes could target Iranian leadership and spike crude oil war premiums.

25
00:02:35.356 --> 00:02:42.157
Four straight weeks of U S crude inventory draws support oil, though rising domestic output caps gains.

26
00:02:42.157 --> 00:02:49.902
Meanwhile, Israel's inconclusive election forces complex coalition talks, keeping Middle East uncertainty elevated.

27
00:02:49.902 --> 00:03:00.221
Historically, late October marks the final dip before a year-end rally, though 1962, 1974, and 2002 proved exceptions.

28
00:03:00.221 --> 00:03:07.072
Technically, the S and P 500 faces resistance at seventy-eight hundred and support at seventy-six eighty.

29
00:03:07.072 --> 00:03:14.535
Breaking seventy-six eighty exposes seventy-six hundred, while Nasdaq futures must defend their five-day moving average.

30
00:03:14.672 --> 00:03:20.786
Chair Warsh warned that no sector is immune to higher rates, including artificial intelligence.

31
00:03:20.736 --> 00:03:27.292
The Fed will hold a special hearing on November 16 to evaluate A I's macroeconomic impact.

32
00:03:27.292 --> 00:03:34.853
Economists remain split, estimating A I boosts growth by zero point one to zero point six percentage points.

33
00:03:34.853 --> 00:03:41.263
In credit markets, Silicon Valley's massive borrowing needs are clashing with institutional risk limits.

34
00:03:41.263 --> 00:03:46.238
Yields on A I project debt have reached double digits as banks pull back.

35
00:03:46.238 --> 00:03:54.290
Five-year credit default swaps for Broadcom, Oracle, and SpaceX surged recently, signaling rising credit anxiety.

36
00:03:54.290 --> 00:04:00.491
This highlights a critical divergence between upstream hardware windfalls and downstream cash burn.

37
00:04:00.491 --> 00:04:09.253
Upstream memory giant S K Hynix posted blowout results, lifting the Philadelphia Semiconductor Index one point seven five percent.

38
00:04:09.253 --> 00:04:16.655
Hynix revenue soared three hundred twenty-eight percent to seventy-eight point nine billion dollars on an eighty percent operating margin.

39
00:04:16.655 --> 00:04:22.647
Its D R A M and H B M capacity is completely sold out through 2029.

40
00:04:22.647 --> 00:04:28.787
Customer orders exceed supply by over two times, with H B M four ramping this quarter.

41
00:04:28.787 --> 00:04:35.405
Hynix also announced a twenty-trillion-won buyback, though that trailed fifty-trillion-won expectations.

42
00:04:35.405 --> 00:04:44.216
Still, its report lifted Nvidia, A M D, Micron, SanDisk, and hard-drive makers Seagate and Western Digital.

43
00:04:44.216 --> 00:04:51.005
Seagate and Western Digital both bounced off their two-hundred-day moving averages on solid industry fundamentals.

44
00:04:51.005 --> 00:04:57.500
Yet after hours, Alphabet's cash drain dragged the S O X X semiconductor fund lower.

45
00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:04.228
Wall Street realizes upstream chipmakers rely on downstream tech giants burning cash and issuing debt.

46
00:05:04.228 --> 00:05:12.072
Elsewhere in tech, K L A beat and raised guidance, while N X P Semiconductors issued soft fourth-quarter targets.

47
00:05:12.072 --> 00:05:19.584
Teradyne broke below its two-hundred-day moving average despite beating estimates, and ServiceNow tumbled on an earnings miss.

48
00:05:19.584 --> 00:05:27.819
Fortinet plunged twenty-two percent despite solid results, while Enphase Energy crashed sixteen percent alongside SolarEdge.

49
00:05:27.819 --> 00:05:35.282
Enphase suffered a thirty-five percent U S residential solar drop, guiding fourth-quarter sales down another ten percent.

50
00:05:35.282 --> 00:05:42.807
In healthcare, Boston Scientific fell nearly six percent after an August cyberattack forced a full-year guidance cut.

51
00:05:42.807 --> 00:05:49.265
Alphabet plunged over ten percent after hours, erasing three hundred billion dollars in market value.

52
00:05:49.265 --> 00:05:58.162
Third-quarter revenue rose twenty-five percent to one hundred twenty-seven point six billion dollars, missing the one-twenty-eight-point-two billion consensus.

53
00:05:58.162 --> 00:06:05.098
Net earnings fell twenty-six percent to two dollars and twelve cents on SpaceX and Anthropic investment losses.

54
00:06:05.098 --> 00:06:12.844
Excluding that eight point seven billion dollar loss, adjusted earnings of two sixty-seven still missed the three-oh-two estimate.

55
00:06:12.844 --> 00:06:20.552
Core search advertising growth slowed to twelve percent at sixty-three point three five billion dollars, missing forecasts.

56
00:06:20.552 --> 00:06:26.434
YouTube ad growth also decelerated to nine percent at eleven point two billion dollars.

57
00:06:26.434 --> 00:06:33.285
Google Cloud was the sole bright spot, surging one hundred three percent to thirty point seven billion dollars.

58
00:06:33.285 --> 00:06:40.147
Cloud operating income hit eleven point one billion dollars, achieving a thirty-six point two percent margin.

59
00:06:40.147 --> 00:06:46.459
However, single-quarter capital expenditures more than doubled to fifty-one point four billion dollars.

60
00:06:46.459 --> 00:06:53.113
Annual capital spending is tracking near two hundred billion dollars, with further increases planned next year.

61
00:06:53.113 --> 00:06:59.204
Consequently, operating cash flow missed badly at forty-two point three billion dollars.

62
00:06:59.204 --> 00:07:05.932
Free cash flow plunged to negative nine point one billion dollars, marking a second straight negative quarter.

63
00:07:05.932 --> 00:07:14.106
Alphabet halted stock buybacks entirely, pushing shares below Berkshire Hathaway's cost basis near three hundred five dollars.

64
00:07:14.106 --> 00:07:21.716
Having broken its technical triangle, the stock enters a left-side buying zone between two seventy-two and two ninety-seven.

65
00:07:21.716 --> 00:07:28.211
Disciplined buyers should wait for selling pressure to fade near two seventy and verify cash flow recovery.

66
00:07:28.352 --> 00:07:36.549
In stark contrast, Microsoft rallied over three percent after hours past five forty, nearing its five-fifty-one record high.

67
00:07:36.499 --> 00:07:44.734
Fiscal first-quarter revenue climbed nineteen percent to ninety-two point three billion dollars, beating the ninety point six billion estimate.

68
00:07:44.734 --> 00:07:52.087
Adjusted earnings rose eighteen percent to four dollars and eighty-nine cents, while net income jumped thirty-two percent.

69
00:07:52.087 --> 00:08:00.163
Azure cloud revenue surged forty-eight percent to thirty-three point two billion dollars, topping internal guidance of forty-five percent.

70
00:08:00.163 --> 00:08:08.080
Crucially, capital expenditures came in at forty-five point two billion dollars, below the feared fifty-billion-dollar mark.

71
00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:16.070
That capital discipline preserved eighteen point six billion dollars in positive free cash flow, more than doubling expectations.

72
00:08:16.070 --> 00:08:23.055
Among the four cloud giants, only Microsoft is projected to maintain positive free cash flow next year.

73
00:08:23.055 --> 00:08:30.237
While this scarcity commands a valuation premium, investors should avoid chasing shares at current elevated levels.

74
00:08:30.237 --> 00:08:37.504
Meanwhile, Oracle surged ten percent intraday after unveiling its long-term financial roadmap in Las Vegas.

75
00:08:37.504 --> 00:08:45.666
Management projected capital spending will peak by fiscal 2028, with free cash flow turning positive in late 2028.

76
00:08:45.666 --> 00:08:53.080
By fiscal 2029, Oracle targets over thirty billion dollars in free cash flow and self-funded expansion.

77
00:08:53.080 --> 00:09:00.972
Management capped new financing at twenty billion dollars through 2030, keeping net leverage below three point five times.

78
00:09:00.972 --> 00:09:08.729
Oracle reaffirmed fiscal 2027 targets of ninety billion dollars in revenue and eight dollars and ten cents in earnings.

79
00:09:08.729 --> 00:09:16.952
It aims for two hundred twenty-five billion dollars in revenue by 2030, backed by its three-hundred-billion-dollar OpenAI contract.

80
00:09:16.952 --> 00:09:26.475
Still, heavy debt, data center delays, unrecorded G P U depreciation, and OpenAI concentration cap upside near one seventy.

81
00:09:26.475 --> 00:09:32.896
Risk-conscious investors should wait for pullback support at one hundred thirty and one hundred fifteen dollars.

82
00:09:32.896 --> 00:09:40.151
In physical A I infrastructure, liquid-cooling leader Vertiv soared sixteen point five percent on stellar earnings.

83
00:09:40.151 --> 00:09:47.234
Third-quarter revenue jumped sixty-one percent to three point one one billion dollars as organic orders more than doubled.

84
00:09:47.234 --> 00:09:54.698
Adjusted earnings rose seventy-eight percent to two dollars and twenty-one cents, while free cash flow jumped fifty percent.

85
00:09:54.698 --> 00:10:01.781
Vertiv raised full-year guidance to fourteen point six five billion in revenue and seven fifteen in earnings.

86
00:10:01.781 --> 00:10:09.416
As shares test the fifty-day moving average resistance, holders should trail stops to the monthly average at two twenty-five.

87
00:10:09.416 --> 00:10:16.597
Power giant G E Vernova grew third-quarter revenue twenty-seven percent to twelve point six four billion dollars.

88
00:10:16.597 --> 00:10:24.416
Orders hit one hundred ninety-seven billion dollars, lifting full-year free cash flow guidance to sixteen to seventeen billion.

89
00:10:24.416 --> 00:10:32.835
However, shares erased a five percent pre-market gain after announcing a nine-billion-dollar acquisition of high-voltage supplier Trench Group.

90
00:10:32.835 --> 00:10:40.359
With physical capacity bottlenecks and a rich valuation, G E Vernova requires patience rather than multiple expansion.

91
00:10:40.359 --> 00:10:44.367
That concludes today's XiaoFang Finance Morning Brief.

92
00:10:44.367 --> 00:10:48.533
Thank you for listening, trade safely, and see you tomorrow.
